    "title": "Array .map()",
    "descriptionContent": "Learn how to use map() to modify array values.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17475,
        "title": "Map",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148321,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If we wanted to modify each element in an array and store the result in a new array, how could we do it?</p><p>One way of doing it is to use a loop to convert values before storing them. This works, but JavaScript has an even better solution.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"array\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"97\" endIndex=\"108\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = [];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element \" /><text value=\"of\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" d = \" /><text value=\"Math\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".max(\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", element - \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage.push(d);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemyDamage</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148322,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>JavaScript has a handy function called <code>.map()</code>, which, when called on an array, allows us to modify each value and store it in a new array.</p><p><code>.map()</code> follows the syntax: <code>arrayName.map()</code>. Let's see how we can call it on the <code>enemyDamage</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"reducedDamage\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"82\" /><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"83\" /><option startIndex=\"83\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"88\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map();\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemyDamage</code> followed by <code>.</code> and then <code>map</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148323,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To tell <code>.map()</code> how to modify each element, we need to pass a function as a parameter.</p><p>We'll later program our modifications into this function.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"95\" /><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"96\" /><option startIndex=\"96\" endIndex=\"97\" /><option startIndex=\"98\" endIndex=\"99\" /><option startIndex=\"99\" endIndex=\"100\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>function</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148324,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Before we can modify the array values, we need to pass them to the function. We do that by adding a parameter to the inline function.</p><p>In our example, we'll call the parameter <code>element</code>, but any name can work.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"86\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"56\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"27\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"38\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" bonusUnlocked = scores.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (element % \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\") == \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(bonusUnlocked);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>element</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148325,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Adding a second parameter allows us to access each iteration's index along with the array value.</p><p>In our example, we'll call the parameter <code>index</code>, but any name can work.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"113\" endIndex=\"118\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" inventory = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Shield&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Key&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" displayInventory = inventory.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" index + \" /><text value=\"&quot;: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(displayInventory);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148326,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In order to tell the <code>.map()</code> function what value to store in the new array, the inline function must <code>return</code> a value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"108\" endIndex=\"114\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"14\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"17\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"19\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" reducedDamage = enemyDamage.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Math\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".max(\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", element - \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(reducedDamage);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>return</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148327,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To simplify our syntax, we can switch the inline function with a JavaScript arrow function instead.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"132\" endIndex=\"139\" /><option startIndex=\"141\" endIndex=\"143\" /><option startIndex=\"144\" endIndex=\"165\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" spriteNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;hero_idle&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;slime_walk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;coin_spin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;door_open&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;boss_roar&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" uppercaseSprites = \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" spriteNames.map(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" element.toUpperCase());\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(uppercaseSprites);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>element</code>, followed by <code>=&gt;</code>, and finally <code>element.toUpperCase()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148328,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>.map()</code> doesn't only work on integer arrays, but on other value types, like strings, as well.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Array\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"this\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"90\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;goblin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;hannah&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;dragon&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" nameLength =\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" enemyNames.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element.length;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(nameLength);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemyNames</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148329,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which JavaScript function can we use to modify each element and store the results in a new array?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\"><code>.map()</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>.convert()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>.map()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148330,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we need to pass as a parameter to tell the <code>.map()</code> function how to modify each element?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A function</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>element</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A function.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148331,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How can we pass the array values to the <code>.map()</code> inline function for modification?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By adding a parameter to the inline function</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">By using bracket syntax</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By adding a parameter to the inline function.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148332,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What can we access by including a second parameter in <code>.map()</code>'s inline function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The iteration index</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The array value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The iteration index.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148333,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What must the <code>.map()</code> function include to properly generate a new array of values?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"2\" correct=\"true\">A return statement</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Syntax to modify the array value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A return statement.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148334,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What type of function can we incorporate to simplify the <code>.map()</code> function's syntax?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">An arrow function</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">An inline function</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">An arrow function.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148335,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What type of array does <code>.map()</code> work on?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Arrays of any type</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Only <code>string</code> arrays</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Arrays of any type.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #16",
            "id": 148336,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Call the <code>.map()</code> function on the <code>values</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"49\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"59\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" values = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" doubledLoot = values.map(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\" =&gt;\" /><text value=\" element*element);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(doubledLoot);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>values</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>map</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #17",
            "id": 148337,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add an inline function within the <code>.map()</code> function.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option startIndex=\"89\" endIndex=\"90\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"91\" /><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"94\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyTypes = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;goblin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;dragon&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lengths = enemyTypes.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>function</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #18",
            "id": 148338,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add the appropriate parameter to give the inline function access to the array values.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"86\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" pickups = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;coin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;gem&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;heart&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lengths = pickups.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(element);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>element</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #19",
            "id": 148339,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add the appropriate parameters to give the inline function access to the array values and indices.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"84\" endIndex=\"91\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"98\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" pickups = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;coin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;gem&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;heart&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" debugPickups = pickups.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(element, index);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>element</code>, followed by <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #20",
            "id": 148340,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code the correct keyword so that the <code>.map()</code> function populates the <code>places</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"100\" endIndex=\"106\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" players = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Archer&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mage&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Rogue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" places = players.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" index+\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" + \" /><text value=\"&quot;. &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(places);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>return</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #21",
            "id": 148341,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code an arrow function that doubles each value within the <code>values.map()</code> function.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"81\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"82\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" values = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" doubledDamage = values.map(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\" =&gt;\" /><text value=\" element*\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(doubledDamage);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>element</code> followed by <code>=&gt;</code> and then <code>element</code>, <code>*</code>, <code>2</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
